From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:55:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 235/342] usb_webcam: a consumer whose team ended with all the
 buffers

The frame generator noticed a killed consumer only when a send failed.
A consumer held by the debugger after a crash took every buffer while
its port lasted; when its team ended, none came back, nothing was sent,
and the camera streamed on with its output taken ("in use by another
application" until the media services restarted). With no buffer free,
the generator now checks the consumer's port and disconnects as for a
failed send.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp     | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp b/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
index 36c5ae4528..4375576655 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/media/media-add-ons/usb_webcam/Producer.cpp
@@ -1091,8 +1091,19 @@ VideoProducer::FrameGenerator()
 		BBuffer *buffer = fBufferGroup->RequestBuffer(
 						4 * fConnectedFormat.display.line_width *
 						fConnectedFormat.display.line_count, 0LL);
-		if (!buffer)
+		if (!buffer) {
+			// all with the consumer: a consumer whose team ended with them
+			// (one held by the debugger after a crash took them all) gives
+			// none back, and no send fails to tell it's gone
+			port_info info;
+			if (!fConsumerGone && get_port_info(fOutput.destination.port,
+					&info) == B_BAD_PORT_ID) {
+				fConsumerGone = true;
+				write_port_etc(ControlPort(), kMsgConsumerGone, NULL, 0,
+					B_RELATIVE_TIMEOUT, 0);
+			}
 			continue;
+		}
 
 		/* Fill out the details about this buffer. */
 		media_header *h = buffer->Header();
